=== D. Rule 602 firm quote (published size, not a hint) ===
published offer 100.02 x 100
602(b)(2): a responsible broker or dealer is generally obligated to execute an order to buy or sell
  a subject security, other than an odd-lot order, at a price at least as favorable as its published
  bid or published offer, in any amount up to its published quotation size
100-share buy presented at the published offer: within the published size? True
1-share odd-lot order: excluded from the 602(b)(2) obligation? True
revised quotation size 50 communicated before the order is presented -> obligation size 50
602(b)(1): promptly communicate best bids, best offers, and quotation sizes
602(a)(3) unusual-market relief may apply under Commission-approved exchange rules
do not write that every SIP quote is a named dealer's 602 firm quote in all cases,
  or that the customer can always hit the full NBBO size
do not apply the firm-quote obligation to odd-lot orders
do not ignore the (b)(3) revision exceptions or the (a)(3) unusual-market relief
do not conflate 602 with already-taught Rule 604 (display), Rule 611 (trade-through), or Rule 605/606
assertions passed: 3/3
