=== E. FINRA 5220: offers at stated prices / firmness of quotations ===
5220 is a different firmness rule from already-taught Rule 602
  this is already-taught Rule 602? False
5220: No member shall make an offer to buy from or sell to any person any security at a stated price
  unless such member is prepared to purchase or sell, as the case may be, at such price
  and under such conditions as are stated at the time of such offer to buy or sell
official .01: under normal circumstances, a member making a "firm trading market"
  is expected at least to buy or sell a normal unit of trading in the quoted stock
  at its then prevailing quotations unless clearly designated as not firm
  or firm for less than a normal unit of trading when supplied by the member
  official in-process revised-size clause exists; this toy is not a Rule 6420 engine
  this toy builds a Rule 6420 engine? False
  a "normal unit of trading" for an NMS stock is the official Rule 600(b) round lot
  this toy invents a 100-share normal unit? False
  official not-firm / less-than-a-normal-unit designation and in-process revised-size clause named? True
no product, broker, or venue recommendation
